course: dictionary
lesson: 9569
title: Strange: the word that means unusual
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Strange» has more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. A strange noise is one you cannot easily explain. A strange place is one you do not know yet. Feeling strange means you feel a bit unwell or not like yourself.
explain: Read «Water looks plain, but it is a very strange liquid.» Plain water does not look unusual, so the clue is in what comes next: water behaves in a way we do not expect. Context tells you the meaning, and you can check it by swapping in unusual.
explain: Strange can also be a warning. «If a strange dog runs at you, do not run or scream» tells you that a strange dog is one you do not know, and it may be dangerous. «Asking what will happen first makes it less strange» shows that knowing more can make something unfamiliar feel less scary.
fact: Strange means unusual or surprising in a way that is hard to explain.
fact: Strange can also mean unfamiliar, not known to you.
fact: Feeling strange means feeling a bit unwell or not normal.
fact: A stranger is a person you don't know.
fact: Water is strange: it grows bigger when it freezes, which is why ice floats.
exercise: «The strange noise came from the attic.» What does strange mean here? | Sweet-smelling | *Unusual and hard to explain | Very cold | Funny and loud
exercise: «We walked into a strange place where we knew no one.» What does strange mean here? | Feeling a bit unwell | *Unfamiliar, not known to you | Very dark | Happy and bright
exercise: Ben says, «I feel strange after the late night.» What does he mean? | He feels as if he is lost in a strange place | He feels excited about the night | He feels very cold | *He feels a bit unwell or not like himself
test: «Water is strange: it grows bigger when it freezes.» Why does the author use strange here? | It is in a bottle | It is wet | It is clear and cold | *It does something we would not expect
test: «If you smell smoke or gas, that strange smell is a warning.» What should you do? | Check whether the smell is nice | *Tell an adult straight away | Ignore it and keep playing | Hide under the bed and wait
exam: Which sentence uses strange to mean unfamiliar, not known to you? | Feeling strange after a late night | Water is a strange liquid | *A strange man stood at the gate, someone we had never met | A strange noise came from the garden at night
